  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n   Central Idea: The solution leverages two-stage optimization with adaptive data structures. First, it generates low-frequency patterns via Fourier bases that satisfy integral and range constraints. Second, it applies adaptive Fourier analysis and gradient descent at a higher resolution to refine the solution. This contrasts with previous pure-local search approaches, which can easily get trapped in local optima.\n\n   Rationale: By combining global spectral search with local optimization, the approach effectively explores both low-resolution templates and high-resolution refinements. This hybrid strategy provides multiple fail-safes for constraint satisfaction and optimization path stability.\n\n   Bottleneck Addressed: Localization and parameter grid inefficiencies. The two-stage approach creates isolated points of failure, while the Fourier-gradient hybrid ensures near-optimal refinement.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n   Representation: L1 length m is variable (default: 256, maximum 1024)\n   Variables: \u03c9 \u2208 \u211d^k, time series bases t_i \u2208 \u211d^m_initial, gradients s_j \u2208 \u211d^m_refined\n   Objective: Minimize C_5 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n   Constraints:\n     - Integral: \u222bh(x)dx=1 => \u2211h[i] = m/2\n     - Bounds: 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 for all i\n\n   Optimization: Two phases:\n     Phase 1 (Fourier fit):\n       Minimize f(\u03c9) = \u2225\u2207_{\u2205}(\u03c9)\u2225_\u221e \n       Subject to:\n         \u222b(\u2211a_k cos(k\u03c0x/2) * \u2146x = 1\n         \u2211a_k, b_k \u2208 [-1,1]\n\n     Phase 2 (Gradient descent):\n       Minimize g(h) = max_k correlation(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n       Subject to 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and \u2211h[i]=m/2\n\n   The resolution transfer is achieved by:\n     h_up = \u2131^{-1}(\u03c9_vectors)\n     Then trim/expand to new resolution\n\n   Solver: CVXOPT with custom projection steps for bounds and integral constraints.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n   Global response:\n     h, c5, n_points \u2192 enforce hierarchy and saving\n\n   Steps:\n     a) Variable m (n_points) via range [128,512]\n     b) Initialize via inverse FFT with random phase\n     c) Phase 1: L1-constrained Fourier synthesis\n        i) Pre-reserve bounds m/2 for Euler deconvolution\n        ii) Use CVXOPT with distributed constraints \n        iii) Apply soft clipping for boundary conditions\n\n   Repair function:\n      def repair_bounds(h):\n         overshot = h > 1\n         undershot = h < 0\n         for i in range(len(overshot)):\n             if overshot[i]: h[i]=1\n             if undershot[i]: h[i]=0\n         # Maintain integral via iterative balance\n         balancer = lambda h: (np.clip(h,0,1) * balance_weights) ...\n \n   Fourier Templates:\n     basis(k) = cos(k\u03c0x/2) defined on [-1,1]\n     n_coeffs = ceil(log2(m))\n\n4. Search Choices & Variations\n   - Initial \u03c3 = 5\u03c0 for slope, dynamic step scaling\n   - Phase schedule: 40% 1st phase, 60% 2nd phase\n   - Gradient pattern: damped Hessian mode, analytical\n     } = (correlation - I_0) / L2_stdev\n   - Random component: seed=42 for deterministic restarts\n\n5. Compute Budget & Robustness\n   - Grad tests: 3 full rounds DFS per solution\n   - Time guard: budget_s * 0.7 in evaluation, others in search\n   - Resolution switch: m=512 as sweet spot\n   - Fallback: last solution that improved or parent solution\n\n6. Validation & Return Contract\n   \u043e\u0431\u044f\u0437\u0430\u0442\u0435\u043b\u044c\u043d\u0435: \n     1. 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 for all i\n     2. \u2211h[i] must be in [512-50,512+50] for m\u22481024\n     3. compute_c5 provides boundary checks\n   Final output: (tuple(h.tolist(), float(c5_rounded), int(m)))",
